# Consumer root expression (caos design/flake-inputs.md, "Consumer root").
# Two steps, chained through a variable:
#   1. MOUNTED — splice caos's std/ into this tree at caos-std/. Nothing of
#      caos is committed; the loader checks the pin below against the `caos`
#      input in flake.lock and refuses a drifted one.
#   2. deepen the mounted tree, so every DEPS line ANYWHERE in it becomes a
#      DEEP-DEPS/<name> mount inside the directory that declared it. That
#      second step is what the tools need: a tool is a directory whose
#      `.caos-expr` names its worker image as DEEP-DEPS/nim (caos SPEC,
#      "Tools"), and that mount does not exist until the tree is deepened —
#      caos-tools/<name>/DEPS is only a path until then. Without it every tool
#      call fails to resolve its image.
#
# There is deliberately no DEPS beside this file. Nothing looks a dependency up
# at the ROOT any more: `run-tool` used to resolve every tool script's image as
# a root-level DEEP-DEPS/bash, and since tools carry their own expression they
# name their own image themselves. A root entry would be dead weight that reads
# like a contract.
MOUNTED=run --base:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d21701e1f9628f56824294d61bb6163945fe12b7&dir=std/flake-input-loader --input-tree:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d21701e1f9628f56824294d61bb6163945fe12b7&dir=std --input=caos --in:@=. --expr=$CAOS_EXPR --output-path=caos-std
run --base:@@=git+https://github.com/Metta-AI/caos?rev=d21701e1f9628f56824294d61bb6163945fe12b7&dir=std/deep-deps --in=$MOUNTED
